{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300837-true-names-given-names-and-chosen-names","id":1300837,"title":"True Names, Given Names and Chosen Names","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-29T07:52:52-07:00","id":1300837,"title":"True Names, Given Names and Chosen Names","content":"Taking some inspiration from the Skulduggery Pleasant series, I've decided to expand upon M20's ideas of true names slightly.<br /> <br /> For starters, in the WoD the &quot;true name&quot; of a person or a spirit is not as simple as their birth name. For some reason M20 thinks that James Smith or Sarah Williams etc. is a True Name. Which isn't in line with the wider WoD's take in the past; there the idea has been that a true name is something a person doesn't know, which is a sort of auditory expression of their true nature. Determining someone's true name is really difficult, and in the case of powerful spirits these names can be very very hard to learn.<br /> <br /> So here's my take:<br /> <br /> Given Name: this is what a Mage was called by their parents, and raised under. It's possible to have multiple given names technically, but the go-to tends to be what you were called in your &quot;old life&quot; as a sleeper. This applies to Technocrats too of course. Knowing someone's given name is a decent connection to them and can reduce the difficulty of a magick roll. Same goes for knowing someone's ID or National Insurance number.<br /> <br /> Chosen Name: this is something that certain Mages take as a way of protecting themselves, or heightening themselves above what they used to be. No one takes Bob the Grand Wizard seriously. Herecles though? Ares? Same goes for Technocrats; &quot;Agent Smith&quot; has a much better ring to it than &quot;Agent Little&quot; for example. Some Mages undergo complex naming ceremonies and go to great effort to hide their Given Name afterwards, and some simply start going by this new name. VAs will choose a name they like and tell people to call them by it. Technocrats will be assigned cover stories and identities in some cases. At my table, for example, it's very common for members of House Shaea to take the surname Shaea to protect certain details of their past, and to symbolize their unity as a house. Essentially these names grant mystique and also some mild protection from abuse of your name in magick.<br /> <br /> True Name: it could be said that to know your own True Name, to fully comprehend it, is to Ascend. Well, that is if you believe in such things, and place such importance on them! To some Mages these are a huge deal. They're mostly important when it comes to dealing with powerful angels, demons and other grand spirits. If you want to make a Fetish out of a Prince of Hell or an Archangel, you absolutely need to know at least a fragment of their True Name! Something as informal as &quot;Raphael&quot; won't do the trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T11:12:23-07:00","id":1300882,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say, to keep in line with the wider WoD's take, that to know one's True Name it's to Ascend because that would make creatures that make use of True Name and can divine them (certain Changelings, Mummies with Nomenclature) to hold the keys of Ascencion (a key that I wouldn't put on the hands of anything this side of a Celestine).<br /> <br /> That being said, &quot;meaningful&quot; True Names are something I always wanted Mage to have.<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes Tradition Book revised had some rules for TN - they were their special advantage much like Do was to Akashicks. I'm not fully satisfied by their take (they're mostly a tool to have/hide sympathetic connections) but they add the very, very, interesting (if not terribly useful) notion that paranoid Mages place &quot;traps&quot; on their True Names (anyone that's researching their TN would trigger the spell). Holly Abstract Charms Batman!<br /> <br /> In M20 True Names are little more than an Instrument, they have power if the mage believes they have (except for certain spirit summonings, for some reason). However, I think that there's potential in the idea, even w/o getting out of the idea that they're just one way of understanding the cosmos.<br /> <br /> *True Names reveal the Nature and other important aspects of the named thing. This may be just part and parcel of the Magick (a way to cast sensory effects), but also explains how to interwove magick and TN. Things that other splats do with Naming Mages will do with Spheres as usual, but for those that have TN as Focus all or most of their powers could manifest as Naming, with all that implies.<br /> <br /> *In WoD it's established that Researching True Names takes time and effort, and indiviuals (as all humans and supernatural creatures are) have True Names that are unique to them. If that creature dies or suffers a significative change (like, say, Awakening or a change of Nature) the True Name changes with them. This is established in Mummy and in other WoD books that talks about them - in fact, it's part of the reason of why Naming magick works in the first place, changing the name changes the person<br /> <br /> *The use of TN in magick connects with potent Mystic Threads, as proven by the fact many static magics are based arround them. But it must be obvious that you're using the Name as Instrument to get the benefit, as usual<br /> <br /> *As a house rule: Unique True Names can be used as a Unique Personalized Instrument, but *only* to use magick targeting the creature that's so named (if it's because names have power, or just because a mage puts a lot of effort finding them it's for the ST to know). If the name changes you need to research the new name to get the benefits.<br /> <br /> *As a house rule: TN are important for many spirits, they are also important for the Avatar. Discovering a Mage's True Name discovers facts about his Avatar, but Avatars are independant of the person (Avatars can follow many Mages along their reincarnations) and thus they have their own Names (the more potent the Avatar the harder to discover the name). Discovering the complete TN of one's Avatar may or may not be Ascencion, but it's certainly important because the Avatar has the keys of the Arete and all magick. Each syllabe should be meaningful, perhaps discovering the first one whats what led the mage to Awakening. If Arcane Experience it's used this could be a good way of getting some for Mages with the right Focus.<br /> <br /> As the secret of the Avatars it's one of the greatest secrets of Mage, piercing the secret of the Avatar's TN shouldn't be easy. No splat Naming power should allow to uncover this mystery (at least below &quot;elder levels&quot;), perhaps a Changeling can slap &quot;and it's a Mage&quot; on a person's Name to Awaken it, but the Name of the Avatar should be a secret deeper than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-29-2019, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T11:14:48-07:00","id":1300883,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> oh yeah to be clear, even if a Mummy were to say to a proper Name-focused Mage &quot;Your true name is X&quot;, it wouldn't up their Arete. Even if they know what it is, comprehending its deeper meaning and significance is what's important. With that said actually knowing their own True Name would be a boon to such a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T12:45:06-07:00","id":1302620,"title":"","content":"a clarification. Non-hermetic mages CAN know their true names. it works exactly as tradition book: order of hermes says. It's just that the order of hermes is the only tradition where everyone has(knows) it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}